<%# The end screen's SHAPE, in one place — frame, card, the two columns, and
    the wordmark that spans them.

    Structure only, deliberately: this is NOT the `mode:` partial that
    shared/_card_component is. That pattern works for question cards because
    all three surfaces render the same widget and the only difference is
    whether the text is contenteditable. The end screen's three surfaces are
    not the same content — the player's actions column is eight conditionals
    gated on live-data URLs plus ~15 data-player-target hooks and
    click->player# bindings, the editor's holds two <input>s the player has no
    equivalent of, and the preview overlay's is a static facsimile. A mode:
    switch would be three templates in one file, and would leak dead
    player bindings into an editor that never mounts player_controller.

    What actually broke was the shape: the desktop split went onto the shared
    .preview-thankyou-card class while only the player gained the two
    .thankyou-col wrappers the grid expects, so the editor's flat children got
    auto-placed across the columns. That is the invariant worth having exactly
    one copy of, and it is twelve lines.

    Locals:
      message:    captured content for the left column (required)
      actions:    captured content for the right column (required)
      card_class: extra classes on the card, e.g. "gate-ty-card" (optional)
      card_attrs: extra attributes on the card, e.g. data targets (optional)
      powered:    render the "Powered by Playverto" wordmark (default true) %>
<%
  card_class = local_assigns.fetch(:card_class, "")
  card_attrs = local_assigns.fetch(:card_attrs, {})
  powered    = local_assigns.fetch(:powered, true)
%>
<%# The frame is what the split measures itself against — a container query,
    not the window, because the editor draws this card in a feed that loses
    444px to the right panel and a viewport rule would hand 44px display type a
    220px column. It wraps the CARD only: on the player, .preview-thankyou also
    holds the fixed .regions-overlay and the compare panel, and inline-size
    containment on that would trap the full-screen map inside the thank-you. %>
<div class="end-screen-frame">
  <%= tag.div class: [ "preview-thankyou-card", card_class.presence ].compact, **card_attrs do %>
    <%# Below the split these two are display:contents — invisible to layout,
        so the card is the single flex column it has always been. Wrappers
        rather than grid-placing the flat list, because half the player's
        children are hidden until finish and auto-placement would leave holes
        where they will be. %>
    <div class="thankyou-col thankyou-col-message"><%= message %></div>
    <div class="thankyou-col thankyou-col-actions"><%= actions %></div>
    <% if powered %>
      <%# A direct child of the card rather than of either column: in the split
          it spans both and stays centred under them. %>
      <div class="play-powered">
        <span class="play-powered-text"><%= t("player.powered_by") %></span>
        <%= image_tag "playverto.svg", alt: "", class: "play-powered-mark" %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
